This product is a Cangjie (仓颉) implementation of the JOSE primitives the
EU Digital Identity Wallet needs on HarmonyOS (JWE ECDH-ES + A256GCM, JWS
ES256, JWK, Concat KDF), modelled on:

    JOSESwift
    Copyright (c) Airside Mobile, Inc.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/airsidemobile/JOSESwift

The JOSE logic is reimplemented in Cangjie with the original Swift sources
used as the reference implementation.

This product depends on and/or bundles the following third-party software:

  - eudi_lib_core_crypto (Apache License 2.0; consumed as a sibling
    third_party checkout, not vendored) — ECDSA P-256 / ECDH / AES-GCM /
    digest / JWS primitives backed by Cangjie stdx.crypto.

  - cangjie-stdx 1.1.3.1 (Apache License 2.0) — Cangjie extended standard
    library runtime, bundled under entry/libs/stdx/. See the LICENSE file
    shipped inside the upstream cangjie-stdx release archive.

  - OpenSSL runtime libraries (libcrypto_openssl.z.so, libssl_openssl.z.so,
    Apache License 2.0) and libsecurec.so, bundled under
    entry/libs/arm64-v8a/ for on-device execution of stdx.crypto.

